---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use | MyRigFoundry"
  description="Read the terms that apply when using MyRigFoundry, including information about technical content, external links and website use."
>
  <section class="info-page">
    <div class="info-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">TERMS OF USE</p>

      <h1>Terms of Use.</h1>

      <p class="info-lead">
        These terms explain the general conditions that apply when accessing
        and using MyRigFoundry and its content.
      </p>

      <div class="info-content">
        <h2>Informational content</h2>

        <p>
          MyRigFoundry provides educational and informational content about
          computers, PC hardware, software, troubleshooting and related
          technology topics.
        </p>

        <p>
          We aim to provide useful and accurate information, but computer
          hardware, software, drivers, operating systems and manufacturer
          recommendations can change over time.
        </p>

        <h2>Use troubleshooting instructions carefully</h2>

        <p>
          Troubleshooting results can vary depending on the hardware,
          software and configuration of each computer.
        </p>

        <p>
          Readers are responsible for evaluating whether a troubleshooting
          step is appropriate for their own system and for protecting
          important data before making significant changes.
        </p>

        <div class="article-note">
          <strong>Back up important data</strong>

          Before making major system, storage, BIOS or hardware changes,
          consider creating an appropriate backup of important files and
          information.
        </div>

        <h2>Product information and recommendations</h2>

        <p>
          Product specifications, pricing, availability and compatibility
          can change.
        </p>

        <p>
          Readers should verify current specifications and compatibility
          with the manufacturer or retailer before purchasing or installing
          hardware.
        </p>

        <h2>External links</h2>

        <p>
          MyRigFoundry may link to manufacturer documentation, software
          providers, retailers and other third-party websites.
        </p>

        <p>
          Those websites operate independently from MyRigFoundry, and their
          content, availability, policies and services may change without
          notice.
        </p>

        <h2>Affiliate links</h2>

        <p>
          Some pages may contain affiliate links through which MyRigFoundry
          may receive compensation from qualifying purchases or other
          eligible actions.
        </p>

        <p>
          More information is available in our
          <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/"> Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>

        <p>
          Unless otherwise stated, original MyRigFoundry articles,
          illustrations, graphics and other original website materials are
          intended for use as part of the MyRigFoundry website.
        </p>

        <p>
          Third-party names, trademarks, products and services remain the
          property of their respective owners.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>

        <p>
          These terms may be updated as MyRigFoundry develops, introduces
          new features or changes how the website operates.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent through our
          <a href="/contact/"> Contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>